{"id": "term:pongal", "type": "term", "schema_version": "2", "labels": ["pongal"], "content": {"gloss": "(1) A dish of rice and dal (or rice and milk/jaggery) boiled together until soft. (2) The Tamil harvest festival (Thai Pongal) at which it is cooked.", "usage_notes": "Unqualified 'pongal' at breakfast means ven pongal; 'sakkarai pongal' is the sweet version.", "example_sentence": "Amma made ven pongal and coconut chutney for breakfast."}, "structure": {"part_of_speech": "noun", "maps_to_id": "dish:ven-pongal", "category": "dish", "lang": "ta", "native": "பொங்கல்", "transliteration": "pongal"}, "provenance": {"source_ids": ["src:hand-authored-seed"], "acquired_on": "2026-09-02", "transformations": ["hand_authored", "migration:v1_to_v2"], "synthetic": false}, "quality": {"confidence": 0.9, "validation_status": "human_validated", "corroboration_count": 1}, "version": {"revision": 1, "created_on": "2026-09-02", "updated_on": "2026-09-02", "status": "active"}}
{"id": "term:puli", "type": "term", "schema_version": "2", "labels": ["puli"], "content": {"gloss": "Tamil for tamarind, and by extension 'sourness'. A dish described as 'puli' (e.g. puli kuzhambu) is tamarind-soured.", "example_sentence": "Add more puli water if the kuzhambu is not tangy enough."}, "structure": {"lang": "ta", "native": "புளி", "transliteration": "puli", "category": "ingredient"}, "quality": {"confidence": 0.85, "validation_status": "human_validated", "corroboration_count": 1, "notes": "qwen7b:accept; gemma9b:accept; corroboration=1"}, "provenance": {"source_ids": ["src:en-wikipedia-org-rasam-dish"], "transformations": ["extracted:claude-code", "promoted:seed-idli-rasam"], "acquired_on": "2026-09-03", "synthetic": false}, "version": {"revision": 1, "created_on": "2026-09-03", "updated_on": "2026-09-03", "status": "active"}}
{"id": "term:saaru", "type": "term", "schema_version": "2", "labels": ["saaru"], "content": {"gloss": "The Kannada word for rasam - a thin spiced tamarind-and-dal broth eaten with rice. 'Thili saaru' is the clear, thin kind.", "usage_notes": "In Karnataka 'saaru' covers both what Tamils call rasam and a thinner style of sambar."}, "structure": {"lang": "kn", "native": "ಸಾರು", "transliteration": "saaru", "category": "dish"}, "quality": {"confidence": 0.85, "validation_status": "human_validated", "corroboration_count": 1, "notes": "qwen7b:accept; gemma9b:accept; corroboration=1"}, "provenance": {"source_ids": ["src:en-wikipedia-org-rasam-dish"], "transformations": ["extracted:claude-code", "promoted:seed-idli-rasam"], "acquired_on": "2026-09-03", "synthetic": false}, "version": {"revision": 1, "created_on": "2026-09-03", "updated_on": "2026-09-03", "status": "active"}}
{"id": "term:sambar", "type": "term", "schema_version": "2", "labels": ["sambar"], "content": {"gloss": "A tamarind- and toor-dal-based vegetable stew, seasoned with sambar powder, eaten with rice, idli or dosai across South India.", "usage_notes": "Also 'sambhar' / 'saaru' in parts of Karnataka."}, "structure": {"lang": "ta", "native": "சாம்பார்", "transliteration": "sambar", "category": "dish"}, "provenance": {"source_ids": ["src:en-wikipedia-org-sambar-dish"], "transformations": ["extracted", "promoted:smoke-1-reviewed"], "acquired_on": "2026-09-03", "synthetic": false}, "quality": {"confidence": 0.9, "validation_status": "human_validated", "corroboration_count": 1, "notes": "extracted (qwen7b) from Wikipedia; human-reviewed"}, "version": {"revision": 1, "created_on": "2026-09-03", "updated_on": "2026-09-03", "status": "active"}}
{"id": "term:thaalippu", "type": "term", "schema_version": "2", "labels": ["thaalippu", "thalippu"], "content": {"gloss": "A tempering: whole spices and aromatics bloomed in hot fat and added to a dish. Equivalent to Hindi 'tadka' or 'chhaunk'.", "usage_notes": "Also called 'thaligu' or 'oggarane' (Kannada border areas).", "example_sentence": "Finish the rasam with a thaalippu of mustard, cumin and curry leaves."}, "structure": {"part_of_speech": "noun", "maps_to_id": "tech:tadka", "category": "technique", "lang": "ta", "native": "தாளிப்பு", "transliteration": "thaalippu"}, "provenance": {"source_ids": ["src:hand-authored-seed"], "acquired_on": "2026-09-02", "transformations": ["hand_authored", "migration:v1_to_v2"], "synthetic": false}, "quality": {"confidence": 0.9, "validation_status": "human_validated", "corroboration_count": 1}, "version": {"revision": 1, "created_on": "2026-09-02", "updated_on": "2026-09-02", "status": "active"}}
{"id": "term:tiffin", "type": "term", "schema_version": "2", "labels": ["tiffin"], "content": {"gloss": "A light meal, especially a South Indian breakfast or evening snack of items like idli, dosa, pongal, upma or vada; also the multi-tier carrier such food is packed in.", "usage_notes": "'Tiffin items' on a menu means the breakfast/snack section.", "example_sentence": "We had idli and vada for tiffin."}, "structure": {"lang": "ta", "native": "டிபன்", "transliteration": "tiffin", "category": "general"}, "quality": {"confidence": 0.85, "validation_status": "human_validated", "corroboration_count": 1, "notes": "qwen7b:accept; gemma9b:accept; corroboration=1"}, "provenance": {"source_ids": ["src:en-wikipedia-org-idli"], "transformations": ["extracted:claude-code", "promoted:seed-idli-rasam"], "acquired_on": "2026-09-03", "synthetic": false}, "version": {"revision": 1, "created_on": "2026-09-03", "updated_on": "2026-09-03", "status": "active"}}
{"id": "term:ven", "type": "term", "schema_version": "2", "labels": ["ven"], "content": {"gloss": "White; plain. In dish names it signals a savoury, un-sweetened, un-chillied version.", "usage_notes": "Contrast 'ven pongal' (peppery) with 'sakkarai pongal' (sweet).", "example_sentence": "'Ven' pongal has no sugar - the seasoning is pepper and cumin."}, "structure": {"part_of_speech": "adjective", "maps_to_id": null, "category": "general", "lang": "ta", "native": "வெண்", "transliteration": "ven"}, "provenance": {"source_ids": ["src:hand-authored-seed"], "acquired_on": "2026-09-02", "transformations": ["hand_authored", "migration:v1_to_v2"], "synthetic": false}, "quality": {"confidence": 0.85, "validation_status": "human_validated", "corroboration_count": 1}, "version": {"revision": 1, "created_on": "2026-09-02", "updated_on": "2026-09-02", "status": "active"}}
